[6] Proof readout
  The triangular/perfect-number idea adds a product-depth carrier:
    p*(Np-1) generalizes x*(2x-1), and the affine a/b words explain
    why order/depth labels matter as much as scalar size.
  Apply it to LRC14 only after exact M/Farey branch and C27/K33 labels:
    p=2 branch -> C27 unit-petal/two-swap splice;
    p>=3 branch -> K33 owner packet plus octahedral/Clebsch side labels.
  Candidate lemma refinement:
    a low-gap non-AP/GW residual should carry an affine-depth packet whose
    unit-visible entries force the C27 petal splice, or whose nonunit
    depth entries expose the K33/octahedral/Clebsch state-lift packet.
  This is not a proof of LRC14.  It is a new labelled packet interface
  and a warning that the false log/quadratic equality must not be used
  as a scalar theorem.
